Depends: libc6 (>= 2.38), libcurl4t64 (>= 7.16.2), libglib2.0-0t64 (>= 2.32.0), libgtk-3-0t64 (>= 3.16.2), pkexec, dosfstools, gdisk
Recommends: ca-certificates, lxpolkit | polkit-1-auth-agent | mate-polkit, exfatprogs, ntfs-3g, parted, syslinux, syslinux-common, udftools
Suggests: wimtools, p7zip-full
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/pbatard/rufus
Description: USB formatting and bootable drive creation utility (Rufus port)
 Rufus is a utility that helps format and create bootable USB flash drives,
 such as USB keys/pendrives, memory sticks, and so on.
 .
 This package is a native Linux port of Rufus 4.15. It reuses the
 platform-independent subsystems of the upstream source tree (the bundled
 libcdio ISO9660/UDF parser, the ms-sys boot record writer and the bad blocks
 scan algorithm) and replaces the Win32 layer with POSIX/Linux primitives.
 .
 It provides a command line tool (rufus) for scripting and servers, and a
 GTK3 graphical interface (rufus-gtk) whose layout mirrors the original
 Windows application.
 .
 No sudo is needed: starting the GUI immediately shows a polkit
 authorisation dialog (via pkexec and a shipped policy file). If the user
 cancels, the application falls back to a read-only mode where devices and
 images can still be browsed and analysed.
 .
 Features: device enumeration, ISO/UDF image analysis, raw (DD) image
 writing with read-back verification, MBR/GPT partition table creation,
 FAT32/exFAT/NTFS/ext4/UDF formatting, PBR and MBR boot record writing via
 ms-sys, bad blocks scanning and MD5/SHA1/SHA256/SHA512 checksums.
 .
 It can also detect processes holding the target device before a destructive
 operation, download official ISO images from a built-in catalogue with
 SHA256 verification, and create a trailing UEFI:NTFS partition so that UEFI
 firmware can boot from an NTFS/exFAT volume.
